course: dictionary
lesson: 6629
title: Context clues: nougat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These words are its context, and they leave clues. «Filled bars are made by laying caramel or nougat as a long sheet, cutting it into bars and passing them on a wire belt through a falling curtain of melted chocolate, with a pool below for the bottoms; this is called enrobing.»
explain: The sentence is about making chocolate bars, and it puts nougat next to caramel. Both are laid as a long sheet and cut into bars, so nougat must be a food that can be cut up like that.
explain: Now check your idea by swapping in a simple meaning. Does «a sweet» still make sense? It does. Nougat is a sweet made of sugar or honey, egg whites and nuts.
fact: Nougat is a sweet made of sugar or honey, egg whites and nuts.
fact: Nougat can be white and chewy, or brown and crunchy.
fact: Nougat is found in chocolate bars and is sold at Christmas in many countries.
fact: French nougat comes from Montélimar, Italian nougat is called torrone, and Spanish nougat is called turrón.
fact: Nougat is uncountable when you mean the sweet in general, so you say some nougat, and a nougat means one piece.
exercise: «Filled bars are made by laying caramel or nougat as a long sheet.» What is nougat in this sentence? | A pool of water | *A sweet | A wire belt | A curtain of melted chocolate
exercise: What is nougat made from? | Pure chocolate and butter | Milk, flour and eggs | Salt and vinegar | *Sugar or honey, egg whites and nuts
exercise: Which is true about nougat? | It is always a liquid you pour | It is a type of wire belt | *It can be white and chewy, or brown and crunchy | It is a kind of bar that is only sold in summer
test: Where is nougat often found? | *In chocolate bars | Car tyres | Garden fences | Shoes
test: Which word in the bar sentence tells you what happens to the nougat before it is cut? | Enrobing | Bottoms | Pool | *Laying
exam: In the sentence about bars, why does reading the words around nougat help you? | Because it proves the word is spelled correctly | Because it makes the sentence shorter | Because the words are always longer than the hard word | *Because the words give clues about what nougat is
